      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. This dose is about twice the immediate-release maximum. It would also carry a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily**, which are common regimens.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away. If you do intend a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the prescriber outside this tool."
      }
